From 19fb22a9f0a1e3c14fe3ae4812fd96a187b22389 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:23:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Django startup, data-root consistency, forecast paths and
 repo hygiene

- config/settings.py: DATA_DIR referenced BASE_DIR before it was defined
  (NameError on every manage.py command). PYRO_DATA_ROOT now means the
  folder containing data/, the same rule core.src.config uses, so the
  pipeline and the views read/write the same place.
- config/urls.py: import include (NameError once settings loaded).
- train_countries / predict_countries / download_firms commands: call
  execute() with the options Django normally supplies; they crashed with
  KeyError: 'force_color'. Docstrings no longer tell users to pass a
  literal `--`.
- core.src.config: add DATA_DIR/OUTPUTS_DIR/CACHE_DIR; stop creating
  data/processed at import time (new ensure_dirs(), called by the
  pipeline entry points that write there).
- core.forecast: train/predict default to DATA_DIR/outputs (what the
  forecast view reads) instead of ./outputs relative to the cwd; the
  country-borders cache moves to DATA_DIR/cache.
- core/forecast/predict_countries.py: restore the original script from
  jspyro (incl. --live-key near-real-time top-up) in place of the
  reconstruction that dropped it.
- Move core/data/aoi to data/aoi (where PYRO_AOI_FILE resolves); add a
  root .gitignore covering the project-level data/ folder.
- requirements: add scikit-learn, joblib, geopandas, and a root
  requirements.txt that includes Django.
- `python -m src.x` references now read `python -m core.src.x`.
- Remove patches/ and core/fix_readme.py (already applied; in git
  history); core/check_run.py uses PROCESSED_DIR instead of a hardcoded
  data/processed_24h path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
